Z||000004||GTFiero1||10-15-2001||05:29 PM||||actually the tornado air system is suppose to be pretty good. i know some one who put one in their 4-cyl coupe and he said that he could feel the difference instantly. It puts a spin on the air being sucked into the engine with no moving parts. once the air is spinning it can wind around corners easily and increases hp and fuel economy. <A HREF="http://www.tornadofuelsaver.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tornadofuelsaver.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||10-15-2001||05:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>actually the tornado air system is suppose to be pretty good. i know some one who put one in their 4-cyl coupe and he said that he could feel the difference instantly. It puts a spin on the air being sucked into the engine with no moving parts. once the air is spinning it can wind around corners easily and increases hp and fuel economy. <A HREF="http://www.tornadofuelsaver.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tornadofuelsaver.com</A> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Travis(1fst2m6) did his own dyno results on one of these snake oil devices and found a loss of horsepower.  Do a search on this and I am sure you'll find it.  He posted the actul result charts so you can see hard and fast numbers from an outside source.   <BR>I watched the infomercial this weekend and it seemed as if every other word was fuel saver, after awhile it seemed like a subliminal message<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-15-2001||06:47 PM||||a vortex IS the most efficient way of moving a fluid through an orifice (just watch water go down a drain, or empty out a coke bottle..)<P>however, the spiralmax & tornado devices, like K&N and other aftermarket filters, only provide an increase if the stock intake is restricting the airflow in some way. There isn't much of anything that you can do to the Fiero V6 intake that will make it flow more air, short of replacing the TB or making it a ram air.. If a car runs the same with the stock air filter and also with no air filter at all, it's a pretty good indication that the stock intake is already as good as it can get.. on some vehicles I have no doubt that a K&N filter will "add" some HP, and who knows, maybe even the spiralmax and tornado devices have some effects on some vehicles.. just not V6 Fieros.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||10-15-2001||10:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>a vortex IS the most efficient way of moving a fluid through an orifice (just watch water go down a drain, or empty out a coke bottle..)<P>however, the spiralmax & tornado devices, like K&N and other aftermarket filters, only provide an increase if the stock intake is restricting the airflow in some way. There isn't much of anything that you can do to the Fiero V6 intake that will make it flow more air, short of replacing the TB or making it a ram air.. If a car runs the same with the stock air filter and also with no air filter at all, it's a pretty good indication that the stock intake is already as good as it can get.. on some vehicles I have no doubt that a K&N filter will "add" some HP, and who knows, maybe even the spiralmax and tornado devices have some effects on some vehicles.. just not V6 Fieros.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ahhh, guess again...<BR>If you have a vortex, or rotation to the "fluid" traveling through a tube, it is actually traveling slower through the tube...<BR>Also has higher friction...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ray b||10-15-2001||10:23 PM||||air flow is a real trip to figure out sometime smooth flow is best others work better with turbluince mostly if change in derections like at valves with the fin up stream in the v-6 head the fin adds turbluence and that adds flow around valves<BR>but smooth flow is better on strait runs.<P>back to cheap mods v-6 ext headers grind out the over hang on the tubes and gut the cat if it is a stick. if a 4cyl get a v-6!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000009||falconhulk||10-16-2001||08:15 AM||||Heh heh the reason K&n "adds" HP is that air flows freer through the material.  The v6 fiero does not run the same with and without a airfilter.  Even if it did the tightly wound cheap ones are proven to flow less air.  By putting the K& N in you just give the engine a bigger gulp of air.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Philphine||10-16-2001||09:55 AM||||i'm trying to learn performance. inexpensive stuff for looks are usually things i luck across. check through the pics of fieros in the gallery to see whats possible. search for the list of cars that use compatible wheel sizes. wings for mustangs-and f-bodies fit good on fieros and there are plenty around if you don't have one or want something different. stuff like that. that way, if you see a deal you don't have to wonder. if the price is right, and you know how you can use/apply it, you can jump right on it.  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mshill||10-16-2001||04:05 PM||||Back on topic... I would say put a stock front swaybar on the backend with poly bushings.  It makes the car handle much better both in the corners and on the straights (mine doesn't wander anymore).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||10-16-2001||04:11 PM||||Find an inexpensive 3.4L engine in a junk yard and bolt it up!  I know it isn't "cheap" like an air filter, but if you can find a good deal on one its still a good bang for the buck... and high on the "bang" factor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
